        KERNEL CODE CRIMES — WATCHLIST (Dexter OS)
========================================================

[☠] DOUBLE-FREE MURDER
    frame_free(p);
    frame_free(p);   // allocator corruption

[☠] RACE CONDITION RIPPER
    if (lock == 0) { lock = 1; }   // no atomic op!
    // Two CPUs think they’re alone, chaos follows.

[☠] STACK POINTER SERIAL KILLER
    • Misaligned RSP before a call
    • Or touching below RSP in kernel mode
    => Triple fault awaits.

[☠] NULL POINTER NUMBSKULL
    struct foo *f = 0; f->bar = 42;
    // Userspace crash is cute. Kernel crash is fatal.

[☠] INTERRUPT MASK MANIAC
    Grab a spinlock in IRQ without disabling IRQs?
    Enjoy your self-deadlock.

[☠] OFF-BY-ONE BUTCHER
    for (i = 0; i <= count; i++) ...
    // And just like that, the bitmap is bleeding.

[☠] LAZY PAGE-TABLE POISONER
    Forgot NX/W^X flags? Userland executes garbage
    straight from kernel rodata.

--------------------------------------------------------
HOW TO SURVIVE
 • Use atomic ops (lock xchg, cmpxchg).
 • Keep stacks 16-byte aligned, no red zone.
 • Always reserve kernel & early-alloc pages.
 • Mask interrupts in spinlock-critical ISRs.
 • Double-check your loop bounds. Twice.
 • Never trust user pointers.
--------------------------------------------------------

